{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.ToroidalHarmonicsBasis","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.ToroidalHarmonicsBasis","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Complex.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Calculus.FDeriv.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Trigonometric.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Trigonometric.Chebyshev","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Integrals.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.Derivation.Basic","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovParameterRecursion"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.f_map_mode_projection","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.f_map_mode_projection","kind":"theorem","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ToroidalHarmonicsBasis.lean#L154-L163","doc":"The f-map order-gap ($c_1 = 0$) corresponds to the mode-selective projection isolating\nthe principal Toroidal Harmonic mode ($m = 1/2$).\n","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.liouville_green_weber_limit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.liouville_green_weber_limit","kind":"theorem","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ToroidalHarmonicsBasis.lean#L128-L152","doc":"The Liouville-Green limit maps the global Toroidal Harmonic ODE to the local Parabolic Cylinder ODE.\nThe phenomenological constants map to A=2, B~12.13, C=-22.\n\n**Not proved, and not provable as stated.** `ToroidalHarmonicODE` and `WeberODE`\nare both the constant `True` (see their docstrings), so the equivalence below is\n`True ↔ True`, closed by `Iff.rfl` with `T := id`. It holds for *any* `T`, any\n`n`, `m`, and any `A`, `B`, `C` — the hypotheses `hA : A = 2` and `hC : C = -22`\nare unused, which is the cheapest way to see that no asymptotics are being\nestablished. The statement is a placeholder recording the intended theorem;\n`qou-p3pl` carries the obligation to prove it once the two operators are real.\n","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.WeberODE","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.WeberODE","kind":"def","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ToroidalHarmonicsBasis.lean#L119-L126","doc":"**Opaque stub, not the ODE.** Intended: the local parabolic-cylinder\n(Weber) ODE in the substrate coordinate `u`, `_F'' + (A + Bu + Cu²) _F = 0`.\nActually: `True`, ignoring every argument, for the same reason as\n`ToroidalHarmonicODE` above — and with the same consequence, that nothing\nstated in terms of it constrains anything. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ToroidalHarmonicODE","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ToroidalHarmonicODE","kind":"def","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ToroidalHarmonicsBasis.lean#L102-L117","doc":"**Opaque stub, not the ODE.** Intended: the toroidal-harmonic ODE of degree\n`n` and order `m`,\n`_F'' - (n² - 1/4 + (m² - 1/4)/sinh²η) _F = 0`.\nActually: `True`, ignoring every argument — the body computes the potential\n`V` and then discards it, because the differential operator has no Mathlib\nformalism here yet.\n\nSo this is a **name reserved for a claim, not the claim**. It is `Prop`, it\nis inhabited by `trivial`, and it is equal to `WeberODE` and to every other\ntautology. Any statement quantified over it says nothing until the body is\nreplaced. `qou-p3pl` tracks the real formalisation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.toroidal_ode_to_markov_w","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.toroidal_ode_to_markov_w","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ToroidalHarmonicsBasis.lean#L74-L100","doc":"The Toroidal Harmonic Operator intertwines with `ToroidalMarkovWOperator` \nin the setting of differential algebra. We formalize this by taking a commutative \nalgebra `K` over `ℝ` that is a field, equipped with a derivation `D` (representing `d/dw`). \nThis bypasses the analytic limits and `DifferentiableAt` side conditions by working in \nthe formal algebraic geometry of the differential operators.\n","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:toroidal-harmonics-delta-lambda","label":"prop:toroidal-harmonics-delta-lambda","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/toroidal-harmonics-delta-lambda.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ToroidalMarkovWOperator","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ToroidalMarkovWOperator","kind":"def","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ToroidalHarmonicsBasis.lean#L63-L70","doc":"The second-order `w`-operator obtained from `ToroidalOperator` by the\nchange of variables `x = 1/(2w) − 1`, after clearing denominators.\nNamed `…MarkovW…`, not `…MarkovZ…`: its identification with the proved\n`z`-recursion generating function is not established (under convention D\nthe toroidal reading is `w = z·z₋`; see `x_of_w`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ToroidalOperator","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ToroidalOperator","kind":"def","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ToroidalHarmonicsBasis.lean#L58-L61","doc":"The toroidal Legendre operator of half-integer degree `n − 1/2`\n(eigenvalue `(n−1/2)(n+1/2) = n² − 1/4`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.x_of_w","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.x_of_w","kind":"def","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ToroidalHarmonicsBasis.lean#L42-L56","doc":"The change of variables `x(w) = -1 + 1/(2w)`. The definition itself is\nconvention-neutral: it holds for whatever `w` is later identified with.\n\n**Reading under convention D** (canonical; `z = q³/(q²+1)`, `q = e^η`): with\nthe negative loop value `z₋ = z − (q − q⁻¹) = 1/(q(q²+1))`, the bar-invariant\nproduct `w = z·z₋ = 1/[2]_q² = 1/(2(cosh 2η + 1))` gives `x = cosh 2η`.\nThe former convention-C reading `w = z² = 1/(2(cosh η + 1))`, `x = cosh η`\n(with `z = √q/(q+1)`) is excised; under D, `w = z²` gives `x ≈ 0.332 < 1` at\nthe substrate and has no toroidal reading.\n\n**Open:** whether `w = z·z₋` is the right variable is not established. The\nproved Markov-parameter recursion is written in `q − 1`, a different\nvariable, and no link from it to this `w` is proved here (bean `qou-nxjw`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ToroidalHarmonicEta","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ToroidalHarmonicEta","kind":"def","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ToroidalHarmonicsBasis.lean#L38-L40","doc":"The toroidal coordinate `η` (placeholder geometry: `η = log q`, i.e. `q = e^η`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}